## Summary

The daemon's **announcement-processing loop** (`src/lib.rs` ~`5667`) upserts *every observed agent* — including its **own** — into the `ContactStore` as `TrustLevel::Unknown` via `ContactStore::add_machine`. There is **no agent-id self-skip** in that path (only a `user_id` filter exists elsewhere). As a result, whenever the daemon observes a rebroadcast of its own identity announcement, it registers itself as a contact.

This was the root cause of the `daemon_api_import_card_invalid_trust_level_rejected` flake (#142): the test asserted the daemon's own agent must be **absent** from `/contacts` after a rejected import, but the background loop intermittently added it first. #143 fixed that **test** (assert provenance: if present, trust must be `unknown`); this issue is the production-side follow-up.

## Where it happens

```rust
// src/lib.rs, announcement handler (paraphrased)
let mut store = contact_store.write().await;
let record = contacts::MachineRecord::new(announcement.machine_id, None);
store.add_machine(&announcement.agent_id, record);
```

`add_machine` has no `announcement.agent_id == self.agent_id` guard, so a self-announcement upserts a `TrustLevel::Unknown` self-contact.

