Closes #470.

## The CAS rule

`persist_named_groups_mutation_unlocked` no longer restores the whole-map snapshot on failure. It captures `before` and `after` (both clones taken under the same map write guard, `after` right after `mutate`), and on `NotReplaced`/`Err` performs **per-key compare-and-restore**:

- `touched` = keys where `before.get(k) != after.get(k)` (complete `GroupInfo` equality);
- for each touched key: roll back to the pre-mutation record (insert or remove) **only if** the live map still holds exactly the post-mutation record (`current.get(k) == after.get(k)`) — i.e. nobody else changed that key since our write;
- keys a concurrent writer changed (map writers that do not hold `named_groups_persistence_lock`: owner-cert verdict evaluation, invite bookkeeping, join requests, Home metadata) keep the concurrent value;
- untouched keys are never rewritten;
- `ReplacedNotDurable` does **not** roll back — the replacement is visible on disk and memory stays aligned with it (unchanged r2 Watson-ruling semantics).

Lock order unchanged (membership mutex → persistence lock → map write).

## Complete equality

`GroupInfo` now derives `PartialEq` over **every** field, including `#[serde(skip)]`/local-only ones (`owner_cert_reverify_required`, `issued_invite_secrets`, `issued_invites`, Home metadata, commit log); `PartialEq, Eq` added to `IssuedInviteRecord` (consumption state included). No tuple subset, no serialized-bytes comparison — a `certificate_missing_since_ms`-o

## Problem

Follow-on to #370. The sole-member-in-being carve-out in `validate_live_to_withdrawn_authority` (`src/groups/state_commit.rs`) returned `Ok` for **any** sole member-in-being with no `action_kind` check. A **Pending** sole signer applying a live→withdrawn commit as `NonMemberRequest` was therefore authorized: `Pending` ⇒ `active_signer_role` is `None` ⇒ the carve-out passes and the ordinary `NonMemberRequest => signer_role.is_none()` arm succeeds, and the group withdraws.

The #370 apply oracle (`expected_withdrawn_apply_authorized`) already forbids this (`NonMemberRequest => false` for any rostered sole member); the product did not match it.

## Fix (design I1 — reject NMR, then carve-out)

Inside `validate_live_to_withdrawn_authority`, after the existing not-a-transition `Ok` and after the `allow_live_withdrawal` check:

```rust
if action_kind == ActionKind::NonMemberRequest {
    return Err(ApplyError::Unauthorized {
        signer: commit.committed_by.clone(),
        action: ActionKind::NonMemberRequest.name(),
    });
}
if signer_is_sole_member {
    return Ok(());
}
```

The existing `AdminOrHigher` / role check stays **after** both lines, so #369 SoleMemberDelete keeps working (`AdminOrHigher` / `MemberSelf` sole member-in-being still `Ok`). No fourth `ActionKind`; the conjunctive-skip variant was deliberately avoided (it leaves the Pending+NMR hole open via the ordinary arm).

